Display and input: brightness race fixed, 90 Hz, vsync from the panel, faster touch reads.

all30 came up dark (lit only during the power-button fade): CoreBrightness's "0.00 nits" on
IOMFBBrightnessLevel landed after AppleARMBacklight's level (all29 had the opposite order).
While AppleARMBacklight is published that property no longer sets the panel.

90 Hz (user): the k7_38_0c_0a panel's one DT timing is 90 frames a second (2432 lines), 60 being
the same clocks with a long vertical front porch. setupRate() measures what INTF_1 sends
(frame/line counters), and with sweetfb_rate (default 90; 0 = leave it) cuts a long porch back in
INTF_1 and DSI0's VIDEO_MODE_TOTAL, re-measures, and restores the old timing if it is off. iOS is
told the measured rate (TimingElements), and the vsync is armed for the panel's next frame start
from the line counter instead of a free-running 16.7 ms timer.

Input delay (user): the touch loop slept 10 ms a pass. Now the IRQ line is looked at every 1 ms
(read at once when low, else every 8 ms) and the chip is read every 4 ms while a finger is down;
sweettouchpoll=10 is the old pace. SweetFramebuffer logs the time from a new finger to the next
swap (first 40).

